    "description": "Let a fresh reading lower the stored usage figure after a partial reset\n\n## Summary\n\nAfter a partial reset of a usage window, the shared usage file kept the old, higher figure until the window ended. On 2026-11-24 it showed seven-day at 99% when the account was at 69%. Now a fresh reading of the account lowers the stored figure in the same window. A status line sample of an idle session, also a repeat of its old figure, never raises it again.\n\n**Ticket:** N/A\n**Type:** Bug fix\n\n---\n\n## Agent context\n\n### Authority\n\n`skills/orchestrator/references/usage.md` \"The shared file\" owns the merge rule. `docs/design.md` §15.162 holds the finding.\n\n### What changed, by file\n\n- `skills/orchestrator/scripts/crew-usage.py`: `merge_window` takes a `fresh` flag, and a fresh reading replaces a window with an equal `resets_at` also when its percent is lower. A lower five-hour figure from a fresh reading starts `window_first` again. `usage.json` keeps the last figure of each window per session id in `sessions` for 2 days, and a sample equal to the last one of its own session changes nothing.\n- `skills/orchestrator/scripts/test-crew-usage.py`: six new checks in R3, each group committed failing first (3 of 4 checks failed before the fix for the lowered figure, then 2 of 2 failed before the fix for the idle repeat).\n- `skills/orchestrator/references/usage.md`: the merge rule, the `sessions` field and the `updated_at` rule say the new cases.\n- `docs/design.md`: new finding §15.162.\n- `CLAUDE.md`: build state says what is built and that only the seeded test ran it.\n- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`: version 0.1.130.\n\n### Constraints that applied\n\nThe rule lives only in `usage.md`. The plugin `version` is bumped in both manifests, because the PR changes `skills/`.\n\n### How this was verified\n\n`python3 skills/orchestrator/scripts/test-crew-usage.py` gives 107 of 107 checks passed, with a stub `claude`.\n\n### Known gaps\n\nNo live reading ran the change. `check` and `watch` take a fresh reading only when the newest sample is older than 5 minutes. A session whose first sample comes after the reset with an old figure is not told apart. A fresh reading can lower a figure that a session raised in the few seconds of the probe, and the next sample of that session raises it again.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZh7PDNExjtW2kbKe69\n",
